      "id": "tokugawa-ieyasu-yamaoka-s365-p48590",
      "source_en": "One of Nagayasu’s confidants brought this unexpected news to Akashi Kamon and also reported it to Hayami Kai-no-kami. Akashi Kamon was, of course, a Catholic who had signed Nagayasu’s joint declaration; unlike Nagayasu, however, he had pursued an entirely different purpose in asking numerous daimyos, including Hideyori, to add their names. Thus, the moment he heard that Nagayasu had suffered a stroke and taken to his bed, an immense unease engulfed him.",
